[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2453824553","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98576#issuecomment-2453824553","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98576","id":2453824553,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SQmQp","user":{"login":"n-l","id":5014024,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMTQwMjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5014024?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/n-l","html_url":"https://github.com/n-l","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n-l/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n-l/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n-l/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n-l/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n-l/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n-l/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n-l/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n-l/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/n-l/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-04T04:52:22Z","updated_at":"2024-11-04T05:16:09Z","body":"This *seems* to only happen when a subresource is involved. In the case of your MRP, that would be the `BoxMesh` of the `MeshInstance3D`, as well as the `BoxShape3D` of the `CollisionShape3D`, which you're updating properties of. When I tried to change properties of a `CSGBox3D` the exact same way, the bug didn't occur, but dealing with the `PrismMesh` subresource of a `CSGMesh3D` led to the same problems.\r\n\r\nThe issue still occurs as of commit `1bffd6c` on the master branch.\r\n\r\nA temporary workaround I'm using is to duplicate the subresource by adding this line in `_ready()`:\r\n\r\n`$MeshInstance3D.mesh = $MeshInstance3D.mesh.duplicate(true)`","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repo